    "body": "Interesting! It's not actually a `<template for>` limitation, but rather a `<template>` limitation in general... \nSomewhat related to #3563 and to [this old mailing list discussion](https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-webapps/2012AprJun/1061.html).\n\nThere are a few ways to approach it:\nA. Do nothing\nB. `<template type=\"html|math|svg\">` or `namespace` or some such, which would change the namespace of its children while parsing. It's probably one of those solution that sound sensible but there is some ancient reason not to do. I'd like us to spell it out if such reason exists.\nC. Fix this specifically for `<template for>`, taking the namepace from the parent of the patching target. This seems straightforward to spec but I don't know if it has some hidden security/complexity implications.",
